# The mouse wheel scrolls the Settings list — the box is 35 rows tall for
# a long list. A notch down moves the top of the list away; the cursor
# follows the window (the row it marks is always visible), and a notch
# up brings the top back.
command view.settings
expect screen contains "── UI ──"
scroll 60 20 down
expect screen lacks "── UI ──"
scroll 60 20 up
expect screen contains "── UI ──"
# A row per notch (Rust's `settings_move_row(±1)` an event): forty-six
# notches carry the UI section past and bring the Editor header into the
# window, at the box's height on any screen the suite runs at. The count
# tracks the section's length, so a row added to UI buys one more notch
# here — 41 was exactly on the boundary until *Confirm on quit* pushed it
# over, and the three *First … colour* rows (accent-defaults) took the
# block from 43 to 46; at 45 the header is still one row below the window.
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
scroll 60 20 down
